<Article><Journal><ISOAbbreviation>Dermatitis</ISOAbbreviation><Title>Dermatitis : contact, atopic, occupational, drug</Title></Journal>
<ArticleTitle>Allergic Contact Dermatitis to Parabens Associated With Topical Roflumilast Cream: A Case Series of 2 Patients.</ArticleTitle>
<Abstract><AbstractText>We describe 2 patients who developed allergic contact dermatitis to parabens while using topical roflumilast cream. Both had positive patch test reactions to roflumilast cream and paraben mix. The first patient improved significantly after discontinuation.&#160; Clinicians should consider excipient allergy when patients worsen on roflumilast.</AbstractText></Abstract>
